cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below and also cite the Panasonic 18650PF dataset."
title: "bmsoc: EKF / UKF / AEKF state-of-charge estimation with leave-one-profile-out benchmarking"
abstract: >-
  A reusable state-of-charge estimator package (coulomb counter, EKF, UKF, adaptive
  EKF) built on a temperature-aware second-order RC model with an explicit voltage-bias
  state. Benchmark on 24 Panasonic NCR18650PF driving profiles from -20 to 25 °C with
  leave-one-profile-out parameter calibration, then transferred unchanged to 24 CALCE
  A123 (LFP) discharge segments from -10 to 50 °C. Reference results: 2.9-3.8 percentage
  points SOC RMSE when the initial SOC is wrong by 30 pp; 1.7-3.1 pp for the adaptive
  EKF; 0.2-2.0 pp on LFP. Documented diagnosis of two UKF failure modes (inconsistent
  unscented weights and OCV clamped outside SOC in [0,1]). Calibration-margin probe
  shows capacity error (5-10 % -> 3-7 pp) dominates the error budget and cannot be
  absorbed by any filter state, whereas a ±40 mV OCV-table error costs 0.6 pp or less.
  Two stress tests bound the validity of these numbers: starting mid-plateau instead of
  full degrades initial-SOC error from 0.6-1.1 pp to 12-36 pp on LFP (a start-point
  effect, not a chemistry effect), and online capacity identification as a fifth filter
  state fails on real data because the 38-53 mV model residual is voltage-
  indistinguishable from capacity drift. The capacity error growth law
  err_end = -(1/s-1)(1-SOC_end) is verified point-for-point.
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-31
